      "claim": "Most anchovy species prefer temperate water temperatures (approximately 10‑20 °C).",
      "evidence": "Scientific studies on European anchovy (Engraulis encrasicolus) and Pacific anchovy (Engraulis mordax) report optimal growth and spawning at 12‑20 °C and reduced abundance above 25 °C.",
